# Covers: a watcher body that unregisters the next watcher in the
# active list must not truncate the rest of the evaluation pass.
# (refactor-4 SCH4-04)
#
# Five watchers observe Realm.go in registration order:
#   P (at)        — idempotency probe, appends "P"
#   W (whenever)  — idempotency probe, appends "W"
#   A (at sync)   — cascade trigger, calls t2.stop()
#   B (at, t2-owned) — gets cascaded (PENDING_UNREGISTER) by A's inline body
#   C (at)        — must still fire after the cascade rescan
#
# P and W are installed first so they precede the cascade watcher in
# active_watchers_head.  They pin that each fires exactly once (no double-fire
# on the rescan).  A truthy WHENEVER is level-triggered under active dispatch
# (whenever_edge_only == 0) and would re-fire on a naive rescan re-visit;
# the eval-pass stamp (eval_pass_gen) prevents this.
#
# B must be live in active_watchers_head at eval time.  Prior to v0.13.5
# a bare `t2: at (Realm.go) { ... }` would cascade B immediately when the
# t2: lexical scope exited (OP_POP_TAG → vm_tag_scope_teardown), so the
# old fixture used `t2: { at (...) B; waituntil(false) }` to keep the
# scope open.  v0.13.5 (v0.13.4-A fix) guards the cascade with
# FLAG_TAG_USER_OWNED so user-owned tags keep their watchers alive past
# scope close; the bare form is now correct.  The D3 "no-active-scope"
# guard in tag_stop_native also snapshots had_watcher before urbi_tag_stop
# so stopping a watcher-only tag does not false-alarm.
#
# When Realm.go rises, A's inline body calls t2.stop().  urbi_tag_stop
# calls pending_onleave_queue_push for every watcher in
# t2->member_watchers_head (B): PENDING_UNREGISTER set, unlinked from
# active list, next_active cleared.
# The pre-captured `next = B` in watcher_eval_dirty now has
# next_active = NULL, so without the fix the loop terminates before
# evaluating C — a silent same-tick truncation.
# The fix: when the pre-captured successor is PENDING, restart from
# active_watchers_head so C still fires this pass.
#
# B never fires: its watcher is unregistered before it is evaluated.
# C must fire.  P and W each fire exactly once.
# Post-fix expected: Realm.hits == "PWC".
# Pre-fix expected:  Realm.hits == "" (C missed entirely; P, W also missed
#                    because the truncation swallows the whole tail).
#
## timeout: 30
## host: run Realm.hits = ""
## host: run Realm.go = false
## host: run var t2 = Tag.new()
## host: run at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "P" }
## host: run whenever (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "W" }
## host: run at sync (Realm.go) { t2.stop() }
## host: run t2: at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "B" }
## host: run at (Realm.go) { Realm.hits = Realm.hits + "C" }
## host: run Realm.go = true
## host: step 100000
## host: run Realm.hits
[00000000] ""
[00000000] false
[00000000] <Tag>
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] true
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] "PWC"
